{
  "@context": "../../context.jsonld",
  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design and fabrication of the oxidizer delivery system for hybrid rocket engines. Pressure-fed systems use helium or nitrogen to expel liquid oxidizer (N2O, LOX) from a tank through an injection plate into the combustion port, suited to lower-thrust engines (SpaceShipOne, 74 kN). Pump-fed systems use a turbopump to deliver high-pressure gaseous oxygen (GOX) for high-thrust engines, enabling higher chamber pressure and Isp. Throttle valves and run valves provide thrust modulation and stop/restart.",
